@@ -0,0 +1,88 @@
+# Iris-3B export (FP8 / MXFP8 / NVFP4 / INT8 tensorwise)
+
+Quantize **Iris-3B** ([`speridlabs/iris-3b`](https://huggingface.co/speridlabs/iris-3b)), a
+3B pixel-space hybrid MMDiT: no VAE, the network paints RGB pixels through a small pixel head.
+Text encoder: Qwen3-VL-4B (separate file, not touched here).
+
+## Supported formats & configs
+
+| Format | Command | Config | Runs on |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| FP8 E4M3 | `export-model` | `configs/iris_3b_fp8.yaml` | any GPU (FP8 matmul on SM≥8.9) |
+| FP8 E5M2 | `export-model` | `configs/iris_3b_fp8_e5m2.yaml` | any GPU (FP8 matmul on SM≥8.9) |
+| MXFP8 | `export-model-mxfp8` | `configs/iris_3b_mxfp8.yaml` | Blackwell (SM≥10) |
+| NVFP4 | `export-model-nvfp4` | `configs/iris_3b_nvfp4.yaml` | Blackwell (SM≥10) |
+| INT8 tensorwise (+ConvRot) | `export-model-int8-tensorwise` | `configs/iris_3b_int8_tensorwise.yaml` | SM≥7.5 |
+
+INT8 W8A8 (the INT8-Fast node) and INT4 are not provided.
+
+## Loading in ComfyUI
+
+**Stock ComfyUI has no Iris model.** The artifacts keep Iris's original bare key names
+(`blocks.0.attn.q_proj_x.weight`, ...) plus the usual per-layer `comfy_quant` markers, so they
+load through a custom node that builds Iris from `comfy.ops` and detects per-layer
+quantization: [envy-ai/ComfyUI-Iris](https://github.com/envy-ai/ComfyUI-Iris)
+(`load_model` → `comfy.utils.detect_layer_quantization(sd, "")`; ComfyUI ≥ 0.37). Put the
+file in `models/diffusion_models/` and pick it in **Load Iris Model**. Loaders that wrap the
+upstream speridlabs code directly (plain `nn.Linear`) cannot read these files.
+
+## Quick start
+
+The release is **float32**, and the exporters copy every tensor they do not quantize
+verbatim, so cast it to bfloat16 first (Iris runs under bfloat16 autocast; nothing is lost):
+
+```bash
+hf download speridlabs/iris-3b --local-dir iris-3b --exclude "depth/*" "upscaler/*"
+python scripts/external/iris_fp32_to_bf16.py iris-3b/model.safetensors iris-3b-bf16/model.safetensors
+
+comfy-quants export-model \
+  --config configs/iris_3b_fp8.yaml \
+  --source iris-3b-bf16/model.safetensors \
+  --out iris-3b_fp8.safetensors --device cuda:0 --hash-output --json
+```
+
+Swap in `export-model-mxfp8`, `export-model-nvfp4` or `export-model-int8-tensorwise` with the
+matching config for the other formats. A fine-tune saved by diffusion-pipe (or its EMA) is the
+same layout: point `--source` at its `model.safetensors`.
+
+The `depth/` and `upscaler/` fine-tunes share the architecture, so the same configs export
+them, but ComfyUI-Iris only runs text-to-image.
+
+## Architecture & layer selection
+
+hidden 2560, 20 heads × 128 with 5 KV heads (GQA: k/v are 2560 → 640), SwiGLU MLP 2560 → 6826
+→ 2560. One `blocks` list: `blocks.0-7` dual-stream (image `_x`, text `_y` weights),
+`blocks.8-23` single-stream. The contract (`model_adapters/iris.py`) declares all 256 block
+Linear weights; it matches the released header exactly.
+
+Default selection (all configs), the same 168 Linears as the community INT4 ConvRot profile:
+
+- **Quantized** (1.39B params): the image side of the dual blocks (`attn.{q,k,v}_proj_x`,
+  `attn.proj_x`, `attn_gate_x`, `mlp_x.w1`, `mlp_x.w3`) and every single block
+  (`q/k/v_proj`, `attn_gate`, `attn_proj`, `mlp.w1`, `mlp.w3`). All have in-features 2560.
+- **Kept bf16**: the text side `_y` of the dual blocks; every MLP down projection `w2`
+  (in-features 6826 is not a multiple of the MXFP8/NVFP4 block size — their export would fail —
+  nor of 16, which the FP8/INT8 matmul kernels need); the shared `modulation_cores`, the text
+  adapter `y_embedder`, embedders, `pixel_blocks` and `final_layer`; norms and biases.
+
+To also quantize the text side with FP8/INT8, drop the three `_y` lines from `exclude`.
+`w2` can be added to the FP8 configs only (ComfyUI then dequantizes it for the matmul):
+remove the two `w2` lines there, never in the MXFP8/NVFP4 configs.
+
+Expected size from a bf16 source: ~4.6 GB (FP8 / MXFP8 / INT8), ~4.0 GB (NVFP4), versus
+6.0 GB bf16 / 12 GB float32. The 1.6B kept parameters (3.2 GB) dominate; quantizing the text
+side too brings FP8 to ~4.1 GB.
+
+## Verify
+
+```bash
+comfy-quants inspect --family iris --model iris-3b-bf16 --out inspect_iris --json
+python -m pytest tests/unit/test_iris_contract.py -q
+```
+
+Validated on CPU: a reduced-width Iris (same key names and structure, unaligned `w2`) built
+with ComfyUI-Iris's model code, exported with each config, then loaded strictly through
+ComfyUI-Iris's `load_model`. Every format loads as its ComfyUI layout and the quantized layers
+reproduce the bf16 matmul within the format's precision (per-layer relative error: INT8 1.2%,
+FP8 E4M3 / MXFP8 2.7%, FP8 E5M2 5.3%, NVFP4 9.3%). Image quality on the real 3B weights has not
+been measured yet: check your own prompts, especially for NVFP4.
diff --git a/scripts/external/iris_fp32_to_bf16.py b/scripts/external/iris_fp32_to_bf16.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b3eb54b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/scripts/external/iris_fp32_to_bf16.py
@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""Cast the released Iris-3B checkpoint (float32 EMA) to bfloat16 before quantizing.
+
+The exporters copy every tensor they do not quantize verbatim, so quantizing the float32
+release directly would leave ~1.6B kept parameters (text side, w2, modulation cores, text
+adapter, pixel head) in float32: a ~7.5 GB "FP8" file. Iris runs under bfloat16 autocast,
+so a bfloat16 source loses nothing at inference; quantizing from it instead of float32
+adds no measurable error (FP8/FP4 round far coarser than bfloat16).
+
+    python scripts/external/iris_fp32_to_bf16.py iris-3b/model.safetensors iris-3b-bf16/model.safetensors
+
+Copies ``config.yaml`` from beside the source. Tensors are read one at a time; peak host
+memory is the bfloat16 output (~6 GB).
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import argparse
+import shutil
+from pathlib import Path
+
+import torch
+from safetensors import safe_open
+from safetensors.torch import save_file
+
+
+def convert(source: Path, output: Path) -> dict[str, int]:
+    if source.resolve() == output.resolve():
+        raise SystemExit("output must differ from the source")
+    output.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
+    tensors: dict[str, torch.Tensor] = {}
+    counts = {"cast": 0, "kept": 0}
+    with safe_open(str(source), framework="pt", device="cpu") as handle:
+        metadata = handle.metadata() or {}
+        for name in handle.keys():
+            tensor = handle.get_tensor(name)
+            if tensor.dtype in (torch.float32, torch.float64, torch.float16):
+                tensor = tensor.to(torch.bfloat16)
+                counts["cast"] += 1
+            else:
+                counts["kept"] += 1
+            tensors[name] = tensor.contiguous()
+    save_file(tensors, str(output), metadata=metadata)
+    config = source.parent / "config.yaml"
+    if config.is_file() and not (output.parent / "config.yaml").exists():
+        shutil.copy2(config, output.parent / "config.yaml")
+    return counts
+
+
+def main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:
+    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__, formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
+    parser.add_argument("source", type=Path, help="Iris model.safetensors (float32)")
+    parser.add_argument("output", type=Path, help="bfloat16 model.safetensors to write")
+    args = parser.parse_args(argv)
+    counts = convert(args.source, args.output)
+    print(f"wrote {args.output}: {counts['cast']} tensors cast to bfloat16, {counts['kept']} copied")
+    return 0
+
+
+if __name__ == "__main__":
+    raise SystemExit(main())
